WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.380
What about turning the Republican party more Libertarian?

00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:06.240
and you know this is something that my colleague Matt Welch

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:08.560
and my colleague Katherine Mangu-Ward,

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:10.880
people at Reason have, we've written a lot about it

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:15.820
and it seemed even a few years ago on the tea party wave and whatnot,

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:17.680
the people who were coming into the Republican party

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.900
were about limiting spending, balancing the budget,

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:25.820
getting out of a lot of social issues as a focus of national government.

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:29.140
Can anything be done to make the Republican party more Libertarian?

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:32.760
Yeah again I think so, but-

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:33.440
You can imagine-

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.440
I can imagine such a situation-

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.920
Now we're deep into like a Rick and Morty multiverse.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:41.920
Right, so like-

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:44.960
In an alternative universe,

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:48.520
I can imagine such a situation

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:50.860
but it's hard to sort of perceive,

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:53.680
like just like it was hard to perceive the whole Trump thing

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:57.960
like that it was going to change the way the Republican party views itself

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:02.940
and change a lot of, a lot of people's positions.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:07.680
I don't know, I think it's possible but again

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:09.860
if you could change the Speaker of the House

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:12.420
and have a Libertarian Speaker of the House

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:14.660
an independent minded Speaker of the House

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:17.820
you'd have a bigger chance of shifting the party.

